foreign  I think my biggest learning from taking  an unconventional path was probably  continuing to be intrinsically motivated  by this sort of curiosity so I think a  lot of young people should figure out  what gets themselves ticking and drives  them  I started a company called alloy we are  a business process automation tool so  what that means is we allow you as a  business user to connect the different  apps you use and essentially automate  work across those apps so what that  means for a brand like Brooklyn for  example is you can connect to your  loyalty platform to your subscriptions  platform so if I subscribe to  pillowcases me as a customer I can  automatically get rewards when I hit say  the 12th subscription renewal so we  actually allow Brands and The Operators  behind them to automate that sort of  work  this is my first company the Catalyst  for starting it is kind of out of just  my personal philosophy on life so I love  saving time I love to optimize  everything in my life so I basically  wanted to make it easy for anyone to do  that themselves without having to code  so when I was younger I actually built a  lot of apps for myself in my daily life  and I realized it's probably not  practical for everyone to do that  [Music]  I left High School a bit early to go  work in Silicon Valley and so I had a  really interesting experience there for  six or eight months I actually went  without really telling my parents and  they we didn't really talk for a bit and  then I applied to Harvard and got in  kind of in an unconventional way so they  asked me for my portfolio of code I  didn't really have a great resume as a  high schooler so I got him purely  because of my extracurricular things and  so when I went to Harvard it was  actually very different from my  experience in Silicon Valley so I felt  like there's a lot of hierarchy it  actually moved a lot slower than I would  have liked so I left after my first year  to work in the valley again and I didn't  expect to fully drop out but I kind of  just never went back so if you could  call it an infinite leave of absence  I started the company when I was 18 and  obviously a lot of VCS a lot of people  we partner with at Legacy companies they  haven't really seen a very young Asian  girl walk into the room unless they're  like an associate or an assistant so it  does surprise people and when I was  starting my career or starting my  company I wore ripped jeans and a hoodie  so it was also very different but I  think it caught people so off guard that  they weren't that like close-minded  I'm grateful that I work in Tech where  people actually respect you if you know  how to code and so I came in with that  sort of background and a lot of times  you actually interface with people over  like forums first and so you don't see  each other's faces so a lot of times  when I was doing business I actually  built up Rapport over email and only  when I kind of showed up in person  people would be surprised  today at alloy were 30 people and we  have a couple thousand Brands using us  and actually we've been able to scale a  lot from great word of mouth on social  platforms like Twitter actually the  fundraising Journey was actually really  tough for us when we started since I did  why I see the accelerator with my  co-founder when it was still in person  and then the pandemic hit in March of  2020 so YC typically has a demo day at  the very end of the batch and that  actually didn't really happen so we  didn't have demo day to help us  fundraise and so I basically had to  learn how to do it while everyone  thought the world was ending so it was  super tough to put together 1 million at  the start of our journey and then over  time things actually got much easier as  we got more traction as the markets got  a bit better so in total we've actually  raised 27 million our most recent round  was 20 million from Andreessen Horowitz  so that was a series A  [Music]  I want my legacy to be of someone who  built beautiful products that made  people enjoy their lives more and in  general I want to be remembered as  pretty curious intellectual individual  [Music]  [Music]

